        <mxCell id="note_text" parent="1" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontFamily=Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=11;fontColor=#34495E;spacingLeft=15;" value="&lt;b&gt;Shared Bus Operational Rules (Sarangi, Section 9.7):&lt;/b&gt;&#xa; • &lt;b&gt;Write Bus:&lt;/b&gt; Exactly one register drives the 32-bit Write Bus per micro-cycle (selected by &lt;i&gt;write_src&lt;/i&gt;).&#xa; • &lt;b&gt;Transfer Multiplexer (3:1):&lt;/b&gt; Controlled by &lt;i&gt;transfer_sel&lt;/i&gt; (0: Write Bus, 1: sign-extended μimm, 2: micro-adder output &lt;i&gt;write_bus + μimm&lt;/i&gt;).&#xa; • &lt;b&gt;Read Bus:&lt;/b&gt; Driven by Transfer MUX output. Any number of registers may latch the Read Bus simultaneously (enabled by bits in &lt;i&gt;read_mask&lt;/i&gt;).&#xa; • &lt;b&gt;Single-Cycle Branch Comparator:&lt;/b&gt; Generates &lt;i&gt;isMBranch = (write_bus == μimm)&lt;/i&gt; directly in hardware, enabling single-cycle &lt;i&gt;mbeq&lt;/i&gt; branch resolution." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="70" width="1380" x="55" y="812" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

